"helpText" = "PasteMaestro combines increment paste, line-by-line paste and matching destination style.\n\nEnable the desired hotkeys in Settings; all are initially off. Defaults: ⌥V increment, ⌃⌥V next line, ⌃⌥⌘C add selection, ⇧⌘V match style. Change, disable or reset each key in Settings.\nIncrement supports numbers, dates and letters, an adjustable step and an unchanged first paste. Revert never overwrites a newer copy.\nAdd selected text to the line slots; ordinary copying does not add lines. Starred lines stay. Select a row and press Return; Option-Return keeps it, Command-Return adds a newline. Select the destination app first. Restart restores added lines. Slots are held in memory and disappear on quit.\nMatch style first uses a matching menu command, then falls back to plain text. Edit menu titles and clipboard restoration in Settings.\n\nCommand-comma opens Settings. Command-W closes the current window. Accessibility permission is required to send Copy and Paste to other apps. The permission section shows status and opens System Settings; permission switches are never changed automatically. Excluded apps receive their original shortcuts.\nLogin launch is off by default and stays quiet. Manual launch and reopen show the main window. Hide from Dock keeps the app visible in Dock and the app switcher while a main or settings window exists. The show-app hotkey works only while running.\nSettings sharing exports, imports and syncs feature options. Login, staying open, exclusions and the show-app hotkey remain per Mac. The original apps and settings are preserved without automatic migration. Any running original app pauses PasteMaestro to prevent duplicate actions.\n\nWhen staying open is on, closing a window keeps the app running. Reopen from the menu bar or Finder; quit with Command-Q or the app menu. Wait for clipboard restoration before quitting. If pasting fails, check permission, enabled hotkeys, conflicts, exclusions and original apps. Processing is local. Sending a key event does not guarantee that the destination pasted successfully. Updates are not configured.";
